# Repository-owned — NOT studio canon.
#
# game-library is a recorded exclusion from the jrmoulckers/.github sync fleet
# (.github ADR-0012), so this file is authored and maintained here. It is never
# synced, and it must not be replaced by the canonical .gitattributes.
#
# `* text=auto` normalizes every text file in the index. The explicit `eol=lf`
# rules below additionally pin the *working tree*, which `text=auto` alone does
# not do on Windows. They cover the cases where a CRLF checkout changes
# behaviour rather than merely producing diff noise:
#
#   1. Files compiled into the binary with `//go:embed`. A Windows checkout of
#      internal/dashboard/static embeds 3,308 more bytes than a Linux checkout
#      of the same commit, so the two builds are not byte-identical and the
#      dashboard's served assets depend on the build host.
#   2. Shell scripts, which fail on Linux with `bad interpreter: ...^M`.

* text=auto

# Go sources and module metadata.
*.go   text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Dashboard assets embedded via //go:embed — see internal/dashboard/assets.go.
*.js   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.tmpl text eol=lf

# Executable scripts.
*.sh   text eol=lf
